[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:Can I Help You, Madam?]
[00:01.18]Did the woman get what she wanted? | 女人得到了她想要的吗？
[00:14.06]A woman in jeans stood at the window of an expensive shop. | 一个穿着牛仔裤的女人站在一家高档商店的橱窗前。
[00:20.19]Though she hesitated for a moment, | 尽管她犹豫了片刻，
[00:23.53]she finally went in and asked to see a dress that was in the window. | 但她最终还是走了进去，要求看一件陈列在橱窗里的连衣裙。
[00:29.66]The assistant who served her did not like the way she was dressed. | 接待她的店员不喜欢她的穿着打扮。
[00:35.42]Glancing at her scornfully, he told her that the dress was sold. | 他轻蔑地瞥了她一眼，告诉她那件连衣裙已经卖掉了。
[00:41.43]The woman walked out of the shop angrily and decided to punish the assistant next day. | 女人气愤地走出商店，决定第二天惩罚那个店员。
[00:48.44]She returned to the shop the following morning dressed in a fur coat, | 第二天上午，她回到店里，穿了一件裘皮大衣，
[00:53.93]with a handbag in one hand and a long umbrella in the other. | 一只手拿着坤包，另一只手拿着一把长柄伞。
[00:59.36]After seeking out the rude assistant, | 找到那个无礼的店员后，
[01:02.76]she asked for the same dress. | 她又问起那件连衣裙。
[01:05.77]Not realizing who she was, the assistant was eager to serve her this time. | 店员没有认出她，这次却殷勤地为她服务。
[01:13.26]With great difficulty, he climbed into the shop window to get the dress. | 他费了很大的劲儿才爬进橱窗去取那件连衣裙。
[01:19.80]As soon as she saw it, the woman said she did not like it. | 她一看就说不喜欢。
[01:25.70]She enjoyed herself making the assistant bring almost everything in the window | 她让店员把橱窗里几乎所有的东西都拿出来，
[01:31.89]before finally buying the dress she had first asked for. | 最后才买了她第一次看中的那件连衣裙，以此来取乐。